/-!
# Strong generation of the perfect derived category, and regularity

Let `R` be a ring. Inside the derived category `D(R)` of `R`-modules, write `⟨R⟩` for the
triangulated envelope of the complex `R` placed in degree zero, and `⟨R⟩ₙ` for the `n`-th stage of
its construction. This file proves two facts about these stages.

The first is a "ghost-map" vanishing statement: a composite of `n` morphisms out of an object of
`⟨R⟩ₙ` is zero as soon as each of the `n` morphisms induces the zero map on cohomology in every
degree. The second uses it: if a *single* stage `⟨R⟩ₙ` already exhausts `⟨R⟩` — that is, if `R`
strongly generates its perfect derived category — and `R` is Noetherian, then `R` is a regular ring
of finite Krull dimension.

Conversely, over a regular ring of finite Krull dimension `d` there is no nonzero morphism between
bounded-above objects whose cohomological supports are separated by more than `d` degrees, and a
perfect complex whose cohomology vanishes across a window of `d - 1` consecutive degrees splits as
the biproduct of its two truncations.

These vanishing and splitting statements feed back into the generation question. Over a regular
ring of finite Krull dimension the stage `⟨R⟩ₙ` with `n` the global dimension already exhausts the
whole perfect derived category, so `R[0]` is a strong generator there; combined with the converse
above, regularity together with finite Krull dimension, the bare existence of a strong generator of
the perfect derived category, and `R[0]` being one are three equivalent conditions on a Noetherian
ring.

## Main results

All names below are in the namespace `StrongGeneration`.

* `comp_eq_zero_of_mem_triangEnvelopeIter`: a composite of `n` cohomologically zero maps out of an
  object of `⟨R⟩ₙ` is zero ([stacks 0FXH]).
* `isRegularRing_and_ringKrullDim_ne_top_of_isStrongGenerator`: a Noetherian ring whose perfect
  derived category is strongly generated by `R` is regular of finite Krull dimension
  ([stacks 0FXI]).
* `subsingleton_hom_of_isGE_of_isLE`: over a regular ring of dimension `d`, there is no nonzero
  morphism from a bounded-above object with cohomology in degrees `> k` to one with cohomology in
  degrees `≤ k - d` ([stacks 0FXJ]).
* `iso_biproduct_truncations_of_cohomology_isZero`: a perfect complex over such a ring splits
  across a gap in its cohomology ([stacks 0FXK]).
* `exists_triangEnvelopeIter_eq_isPerfect_of_isRegularRing`: over a regular ring of finite Krull
  dimension, some stage `⟨R⟩ₙ` is the whole perfect derived category ([stacks 0FXL]).
* `isRegularRing_and_ringKrullDim_ne_top_iff_hasStrongGenerator_iff_regularModule`: for a
  Noetherian ring, regularity with finite Krull dimension, the existence of a strong generator of
  the perfect derived category, and `R[0]` being one are equivalent ([stacks 0FXM]).

## Implementation notes

A chain of `n` morphisms is represented by `CategoryTheory.ComposableArrows _ n`. Mathlib numbers
the stages of a triangulated envelope by the number of extensions used, starting at zero, so the
source's `⟨R⟩ₙ` is `ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter _ (n - 1)`; correspondingly, Mathlib's stage
`n` is the source's `⟨R⟩_(n + 1)`.

Finite Krull dimension is stated as `ringKrullDim R ≠ ⊤`. This admits the zero ring, whose Krull
dimension is `⊥` rather than a natural number. In [stacks 0FXJ] and [stacks 0FXK] the dimension is
instead a fixed natural number `d` with `ringKrullDim R = d`, and the equality with a direct sum of
[stacks 0FXK] is recorded as a nonempty categorical isomorphism with a biproduct.

The perfect derived category is the object property `StacksDraft.Perfect.IsPerfect` on
`DerivedCategory (ModuleCat R)`; that it is the triangulated envelope of `R[0]`, which is what
makes equality with a finite stage express strong generation, is [stacks 0ATI]. An object `E`
strongly generates when one finite stage of the envelope of its singleton is exactly this
property, so [stacks 0FXM] is stated with the three conditions spelled out as `let`-bound
propositions rather than through an auxiliary definition.

## References

* [Kelly]
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FXH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FXH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FXI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FXI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FXJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FXJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FXK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FXK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FXL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FXL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FXM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FXM)
-/

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Preadditive
  CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated CategoryTheory.Abelian

namespace StrongGeneration

universe u v w

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-! ## Detecting zero morphisms out of a shifted copy of the ring -/

section GhostDetect

variable {R : Type u} [Ring R]

private lemma projective_R : Projective (ModuleCat.of R R) := by
  apply ModuleCat.projective_of_free (Module.Free.chooseBasis R R)

/-- A chain map out of `R` placed in degree `p` which is zero on degree-`p` homology is
null-homotopic: a nullhomotopy is produced by lifting through the cycles of the target. -/
private lemma chainMap_from_single_eq_zero
    (p : ℤ) (L : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℤ)
    (f : (CochainComplex.singleFunctor _ p).obj (ModuleCat.of R R) ⟶ L)
    (hf : HomologicalComplex.homologyMap f p = 0) :
    (HomotopyCategory.quotient _ _).map f = 0 := by
  let eX := HomologicalComplex.singleObjXSelf (ComplexShape.up ℤ) p (ModuleCat.of R R)
  let α : ModuleCat.of R R ⟶ L.X p := eX.inv ≫ f.f p
  have hcycle : α ≫ L.d p (p + 1) = 0 := by
    dsimp [α]
    rw [Category.assoc, f.comm]
    simp
  let z : ModuleCat.of R R ⟶ L.cycles p :=
    L.liftCycles α (p + 1) (by simp) hcycle
  have hz : z ≫ L.homologyπ p = 0 := by
    have he : z = (HomologicalComplex.singleObjCyclesSelfIso
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ) p (ModuleCat.of R R)).inv ≫
          HomologicalComplex.cyclesMap f p := by
      apply (cancel_mono (L.iCycles p)).1
      rw [L.liftCycles_i, Category.assoc, HomologicalComplex.cyclesMap_i]
      show eX.inv ≫ f.f p =
        ((HomologicalComplex.singleObjCyclesSelfIso
          (ComplexShape.up ℤ) p (ModuleCat.of R R)).inv ≫
          ((HomologicalComplex.single (ModuleCat R) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) p).obj
            (ModuleCat.of R R)).iCycles p) ≫ f.f p
      simp [eX]
    rw [he, Category.assoc, ← HomologicalComplex.homologyπ_naturality, hf]
    simp
  let S := ShortComplex.mk (L.toCycles (p - 1) p) (L.homologyπ p)
    (L.toCycles_comp_homologyπ (p - 1) p)
  have hS : S.Exact := ShortComplex.exact_of_g_is_cokernel _
      (L.homologyIsCokernel (p - 1) p (by simp))
  let : Projective (ModuleCat.of R R) := projective_R
  let g : ModuleCat.of R R ⟶ L.X (p - 1) := hS.liftFromProjective z hz
  have hg : g ≫ L.d (p - 1) p = α := by
    rw [← L.toCycles_i (p - 1) p, ← Category.assoc]
    show (hS.liftFromProjective z hz ≫ S.f) ≫ L.iCycles p = _
    rw [ShortComplex.Exact.liftFromProjective_comp]
    exact L.liftCycles_i _ _ _ _
  rw [HomotopyCategory.quotient_map_eq_zero_iff]
  let γ := CochainComplex.HomComplex.Cochain.fromSingleMk g
    (show p + (-1 : ℤ) = p - 1 by omega)
  exact ⟨(CochainComplex.HomComplex.Cochain.equivHomotopy _ _).symm
    ⟨γ, by
      apply (CochainComplex.HomComplex.Cochain.fromSingleEquiv
        (show p + 0 = p by simp)).injective
      simp only [map_add]
      show (CochainComplex.HomComplex.Cochain.fromSingleEquiv
        (show p + 0 = p by simp)) (CochainComplex.HomComplex.Cochain.ofHom f) =
          (CochainComplex.HomComplex.Cochain.fromSingleEquiv
            (show p + 0 = p by simp))
            (CochainComplex.HomComplex.δ (-1) 0 γ) + 0
      simp only [add_zero]
      dsimp [γ]
      rw [CochainComplex.HomComplex.Cochain.δ_fromSingleMk g
        (show p + (-1 : ℤ) = p - 1 by omega) 0 p (by omega)]
      rw [CochainComplex.HomComplex.Cochain.fromSingleEquiv_fromSingleMk]
      show eX.inv ≫ f.f p = g ≫ L.d (p - 1) p
      exact hg.symm⟩⟩

/-- A morphism in `D(R)` out of `R` placed in degree `p` which vanishes on degree-`p` cohomology
is itself zero, because that complex is K-projective.

Stated at an arbitrary model `[HasDerivedCategory.{w} (ModuleCat.{u} R)]` rather than at the
file's ambient `CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard`: the argument uses only
`DerivedCategory.Q.objPreimage`, `DerivedCategory.quotientCompQhIso`,
`CochainComplex.IsKProjective.Qh_map_bijective` and `DerivedCategory.homologyFunctorFactors`,
every one of which Mathlib states for an arbitrary chosen derived category. Consumers that need
`D(R)` with `R`-small morphisms — Brown representability asks for coproducts, which the standard
model of `D(ModuleCat R)` does not have at its own morphism universe — can instantiate this at
`ModuleCat.hasDerivedCategory` (`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/DerivedTilde/Basic.lean`), and a
statement proved only at the standard model says nothing about theirs. -/
private lemma derived_single_map_eq_zero [HasDerivedCategory.{w} (ModuleCat.{u} R)]
    (p : ℤ) {Y : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)}
    (f : (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat R) p).obj (ModuleCat.of R R) ⟶ Y)
    (hf : (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat R) p).map f = 0) : f = 0 := by
  let K := (CochainComplex.singleFunctor (ModuleCat R) p).obj (ModuleCat.of R R)
  let : Projective (ModuleCat.of R R) := projective_R
  have (n : ℤ) : Projective (K.X n) := by
    show Projective (((HomologicalComplex.single (ModuleCat R) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) p).obj
      (ModuleCat.of R R)).X n)
    infer_instance
  let : K.IsKProjective := CochainComplex.isKProjective_of_projective K p
  let L := (DerivedCategory.Q (C := ModuleCat R)).objPreimage Y
  let eY := (DerivedCategory.Q (C := ModuleCat R)).objObjPreimageIso Y
  let e := DerivedCategory.quotientCompQhIso (ModuleCat R)
  let q := HomotopyCategory.quotient (ModuleCat R) (ComplexShape.up ℤ)
  let t : DerivedCategory.Qh.obj (q.obj K) ⟶ DerivedCategory.Qh.obj (q.obj L) :=
    e.hom.app K ≫ f ≫ eY.inv ≫ e.inv.app L
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ :=
    (CochainComplex.IsKProjective.Qh_map_bijective K (q.obj L)).surjective t
  obtain ⟨φ, hφ⟩ := q.map_surjective g
  have hQ : (DerivedCategory.Q (C := ModuleCat R)).map φ = f ≫ eY.inv := by
    apply (cancel_epi (e.hom.app K)).1
    apply (cancel_mono (e.inv.app L)).1
    simp only [← Category.assoc]
    rw [← e.hom.naturality φ]
    simp only [Category.assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id_app, Category.comp_id]
    show DerivedCategory.Qh.map (q.map φ) = t
    rw [hφ, hg]
  have hφH : HomologicalComplex.homologyMap φ p = 0 := by
    apply (cancel_epi ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctorFactors (ModuleCat R) p).hom.app K)).1
    rw [← DerivedCategory.homologyFunctorFactors_hom_naturality, hQ]
    simp only [Functor.map_comp, hf, zero_comp]
    exact comp_zero.symm
  have hφ0 := chainMap_from_single_eq_zero p L φ hφH
  have hQ0 : (DerivedCategory.Q (C := ModuleCat R)).map φ = 0 := by
    apply (cancel_epi (e.hom.app K)).1
    apply (cancel_mono (e.inv.app L)).1
    rw [← e.hom.naturality φ]
    simp [hφ0]
  rw [hQ] at hQ0
  exact (cancel_mono eY.inv).1 (by simpa using hQ0)

/-- The property of an object that every morphism out of it which is zero on cohomology in every
degree is itself zero. -/
private abbrev ghostDetect : ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)) :=
  fun X => ∀ {Y} (f : X ⟶ Y),
    (∀ j : ℤ, (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat R) j).map f = 0) → f = 0

private lemma ghostDetect_iso {X Y : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)}
    (e : X ≅ Y) (hX : ghostDetect (R := R) X) : ghostDetect (R := R) Y := by
  intro Z f hf
  apply (cancel_epi e.hom).1
  simpa using hX (e.hom ≫ f) (by intro j; simp [Functor.map_comp, hf j])

/-- A morphism out of a retract is zero as soon as its precomposition with the retraction is. -/
private lemma eq_zero_of_retract_comp_eq_zero {C : Type*} [Category C] [Preadditive C]
    {X Y Z : C} (r : Retract X Y) (f : X ⟶ Z) (h : r.r ≫ f = 0) : f = 0 := by
  rw [← Category.id_comp f, ← r.retract, Category.assoc, h, comp_zero]

private lemma ghostDetect_retract {X Y : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)}
    (r : Retract X Y) (hY : ghostDetect (R := R) Y) : ghostDetect (R := R) X := by
  intro Z f hf
  exact eq_zero_of_retract_comp_eq_zero r f
    (hY (r.r ≫ f) (by intro j; simp [Functor.map_comp, hf j]))

private lemma ghostDetect_biprod {X Y : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)}
    [HasBinaryBiproduct X Y]
    (hX : ghostDetect (R := R) X) (hY : ghostDetect (R := R) Y) :
    ghostDetect (R := R) (X ⊞ Y) := by
  intro Z f hf
  apply biprod.hom_ext' f 0
  · simpa using hX (biprod.inl ≫ f) (by intro j; simp [Functor.map_comp, hf j])
  · simpa using hY (biprod.inr ≫ f) (by intro j; simp [Functor.map_comp, hf j])

private lemma ghostDetect_single_shift (a : ℤ) :
    ghostDetect (R := R)
      (((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat R) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of R R))⟦a⟧) := by
  let e := ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctors (ModuleCat R)).shiftIso a (-a) 0
    (by simp : a + -a = 0)).app (ModuleCat.of R R)
  apply ghostDetect_iso e.symm
  intro Z f hf
  exact derived_single_map_eq_zero (-a) f (hf (-a))

private lemma ghostDetect_binaryLimit
    (F : Discrete WalkingPair ⥤ DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)) [HasLimit F]
    (hF : ∀ j, ghostDetect (R := R) (F.obj j)) :
    ghostDetect (R := R) (limit F) := by
  let X := F.obj ⟨WalkingPair.left⟩
  let Y := F.obj ⟨WalkingPair.right⟩
  let : HasBinaryBiproduct X Y := inferInstance
  let w : F ≅ Discrete.functor (pairFunction X Y) :=
    Discrete.natIso (fun ⟨j⟩ => eqToIso (by cases j <;> rfl))
  let e := IsLimit.conePointsIsoOfNatIso (limit.isLimit F)
    (BinaryBiproduct.isLimit X Y) w
  intro Z f hf
  exact (ghostDetect_iso e.symm
    (ghostDetect_biprod (hF ⟨WalkingPair.left⟩) (hF ⟨WalkingPair.right⟩))) f hf

private lemma ghostDetect_of_mem_envelope_zero
    {X : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)}
    (hX : ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter
      (ObjectProperty.singleton
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat R) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of R R)))
      0 X) : ghostDetect (R := R) X := by
  let P : ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat R)) :=
    ObjectProperty.singleton
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat R) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of R R))
  have : (ghostDetect (R := R)).IsClosedUnderIsomorphisms :=
    ⟨fun e h => ghostDetect_iso e h⟩
  have : (ghostDetect (R := R)).IsClosedUnderLimitsOfShape (Discrete WalkingPair) :=
    ObjectProperty.IsClosedUnderLimitsOfShape.mk' (by
      rintro X ⟨F, hF⟩
      exact ghostDetect_binaryLimit F hF)
  have hShift : P.shiftClosure ℤ ≤ ghostDetect (R := R) := by
    intro Y hY
    obtain ⟨Z, a, e, hZ⟩ := hY
    change P Z at hZ
    obtain rfl := (ObjectProperty.singleton_iff _ _).mp hZ
    exact ghostDetect_iso e.symm (ghostDetect_single_shift a)
  have hBinary : (P.shiftClosure ℤ).binaryProductsClosure ≤ ghostDetect (R := R) :=
    ObjectProperty.limitsClosure_le hShift
  rw [ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter_zero] at hX
  obtain ⟨Y, hY, ⟨r⟩⟩ := hX
  intro T f hf
  exact (ghostDetect_retract r (hBinary Y hY)) f hf

/-- Dropping the first object of a chain of cohomologically zero maps and prepending any map
followed by the old first map gives again a chain of cohomologically zero maps. -/
private lemma homology_map_precomp_δ₀_eq_zero {n : ℕ}
    (F : ComposableArrows (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)) (n + 1))
    {X : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)} (g : X ⟶ F.left)
    (hF : ∀ (i : ℕ) (_ : i < n + 1) (j : ℤ),
      (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat R) j).map (F.map' i (i + 1)) = 0)
    (k : ℕ) (hk : k < n + 1) (j : ℤ) :
    (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat R) j).map
      ((F.δ₀.precomp (g ≫ F.map' 0 1)).map' k (k + 1)) = 0 := by
  cases k with
  | zero =>
      change (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat R) j).map (g ≫ F.map' 0 1) = 0
      rw [Functor.map_comp, hF 0 (by omega) j, comp_zero]
  | succ k => exact hF (k + 1) hk j

private theorem ghostComposite_of_mem_iter : ∀ (m : ℕ)
    (F : ComposableArrows (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)) (m + 1)),
    ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter
      (ObjectProperty.singleton
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat R) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of R R)))
      m F.left →
    (∀ (i : ℕ) (_ : i < m + 1) (j : ℤ),
      (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat R) j).map (F.map' i (i + 1)) = 0) →
    F.hom = 0 := by
  intro m
  induction m with
  | zero =>
      intro F hX hF
      apply (ghostDetect_of_mem_envelope_zero hX) F.hom
      intro j
      simpa [ComposableArrows.hom] using hF 0 (by omega) j
  | succ m ih =>
      intro F hX hF
      let P : ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat R)) :=
        ObjectProperty.singleton
          ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat R) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of R R))
      change P.triangEnvelopeIter (m + 1) F.left at hX
      rw [ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter_succ] at hX
      obtain ⟨W, hW, ⟨r⟩⟩ := hX
      obtain ⟨A, B, i, p, q, hT, hA, hB⟩ := hW
      let G := F.δ₀.precomp (r.r ≫ F.map' 0 1)
      have hG := homology_map_precomp_δ₀_eq_zero F r.r hF
      have hA' : ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter P 0 A := by
        simpa [ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter_zero] using hA
      have hi : i ≫ G.map' 0 1 = 0 := by
        apply (ghostDetect_of_mem_envelope_zero hA')
        intro j
        rw [Functor.map_comp, hG 0 (by omega) j, comp_zero]
      obtain ⟨h, hh⟩ := Pretriangulated.Triangle.yoneda_exact₂
        (Pretriangulated.Triangle.mk i p q) hT
        (G.map' 0 1) hi
      let H := (G.δ₀.δ₀).precomp (h ≫ G.map' 1 2)
      have hH := homology_map_precomp_δ₀_eq_zero G.δ₀ h fun i hi j => hG (i + 1) (by omega) j
      have hH0 : H.hom = 0 := ih H hB hH
      have hG0 : G.hom = 0 := by
        show G.map' 0 (m + 2) = 0
        rw [G.map'_comp 0 1 (m + 2), hh, G.map'_comp 1 2 (m + 2)]
        have hEq : (p ≫ h) ≫ (G.map' 1 2 ≫ G.map' 2 (m + 2)) =
            p ≫ H.hom := by
          have hHhom : H.hom = (h ≫ G.map' 1 2) ≫ G.map' 2 (m + 2) := by
            show H.map' 0 (m + 1) = _
            rw [H.map'_comp 0 1 (m + 1)]
            rfl
          rw [hHhom]
          simp only [Category.assoc]
          rfl
        show (p ≫ h) ≫ (G.map' 1 2 ≫ G.map' 2 (m + 2)) = 0
        rw [hEq, hH0, comp_zero]
        rfl
      have hF0 : r.r ≫ F.hom = 0 := by
        show r.r ≫ F.map' 0 (m + 2) = 0
        rw [F.map'_comp 0 1 (m + 2)]
        change (r.r ≫ F.map' 0 1) ≫ F.map' 1 (m + 2) = 0 at hG0
        simpa only [Category.assoc] using hG0
      exact eq_zero_of_retract_comp_eq_zero r F.hom hF0

/-- **Stacks 0FXH**.
If `K` belongs to `⟨R⟩ₙ` in the derived category of a ring and a chain of `n` morphisms beginning
at `K` induces the zero map on cohomology in every degree, then the composite of the chain is
zero. -/
@[stacks 0FXH]
theorem comp_eq_zero_of_mem_triangEnvelopeIter
    {R : Type u} [Ring R] (n : ℕ) (hn : 0 < n)
    (F : ComposableArrows (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)) n)
    (hFleft :
      ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter
        (ObjectProperty.singleton
          ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of R R)))
        (n - 1) F.left)
    (hF : ∀ (i : ℕ) (_ : i < n) (j : ℤ),
      (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) j).map (F.map' i (i + 1)) = 0) :
    F.hom = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_succ_of_ne_zero (by omega : n ≠ 0)
  simpa using (ghostComposite_of_mem_iter (R := R) m F (by simpa using hFleft) (by
    intro i hi j
    exact hF i (by omega) j))

end GhostDetect

/-! ## Ghost composites and regularity -/

section Ghosts

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [Abelian C]

/-- A composite of `n` cohomologically zero morphisms, followed by an arbitrary morphism. -/
private def IsGhostComposite : (n : ℕ) → {X Y : DerivedCategory C} → (X ⟶ Y) → Prop
  | 0, _, _, _ => True
  | n + 1, X, Y, f => ∃ (Z : DerivedCategory C) (g : X ⟶ Z) (h : Z ⟶ Y),
      (∀ i : ℤ, (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C i).map g = 0) ∧
      IsGhostComposite n h ∧ g ≫ h = f

private lemma IsGhostComposite.postcomp {n : ℕ} {X Y Z : DerivedCategory C}
    {f : X ⟶ Y} (hf : IsGhostComposite n f) (g : Y ⟶ Z) :
    IsGhostComposite n (f ≫ g) := by
  induction n generalizing X Y Z with
  | zero => trivial
  | succ n ih =>
    obtain ⟨T, a, b, ha, hb, rfl⟩ := hf
    exact ⟨T, a, b ≫ g, ha, ih hb g, (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm⟩

private lemma IsGhostComposite.precomp {n : ℕ} {X Y Z : DerivedCategory C}
    {f : Y ⟶ Z} (hf : IsGhostComposite n f) (g : X ⟶ Y) :
    IsGhostComposite n (g ≫ f) := by
  cases n with
  | zero => trivial
  | succ n =>
    obtain ⟨T, a, b, ha, hb, rfl⟩ := hf
    refine ⟨T, g ≫ a, b, ?_, hb, Category.assoc _ _ _⟩
    intro i
    simp only [Functor.map_comp, ha i, comp_zero]

private lemma IsGhostComposite.shift {n : ℕ} {X Y : DerivedCategory C}
    {f : X ⟶ Y} (hf : IsGhostComposite n f) (k : ℤ) :
    IsGhostComposite n (f⟦k⟧') := by
  induction n generalizing X Y with
  | zero => trivial
  | succ n ih =>
    obtain ⟨Z, g, h, hg, hh, rfl⟩ := hf
    refine ⟨Z⟦k⟧, g⟦k⟧', h⟦k⟧', ?_, ih hh, (Functor.map_comp _ _ _).symm⟩
    intro i
    let e := Functor.ShiftSequence.shiftIso
      (F := DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C 0) k i (k + i) rfl
    have he := e.hom.naturality g
    change (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C i).map (g⟦k⟧') ≫ e.hom.app Z =
      e.hom.app X ≫ (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C (k + i)).map g at he
    rw [hg, comp_zero] at he
    exact (cancel_mono (e.hom.app Z)).1 (by simpa using he)

private lemma precomp_hom {n : ℕ} (F : ComposableArrows (DerivedCategory C) n)
    {X : DerivedCategory C} (f : X ⟶ F.left) :
    (F.precomp f).hom = f ≫ F.hom := by
  cases n with
  | zero =>
    show f = f ≫ F.map (𝟙 _)
    rw [F.map_id, Category.comp_id]
  | succ n => rfl

private lemma IsGhostComposite.exists_composableArrows {n : ℕ}
    {X Y : DerivedCategory C} {f : X ⟶ Y} (hf : IsGhostComposite n f) :
    ∃ (F : ComposableArrows (DerivedCategory C) n) (e : X ≅ F.left) (g : F.right ⟶ Y),
      e.hom ≫ F.hom ≫ g = f ∧
      ∀ (i : ℕ) (hi : i < n) (j : ℤ),
        (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C j).map (F.map' i (i + 1)) = 0 := by
  induction n generalizing X Y with
  | zero =>
    refine ⟨ComposableArrows.mk₀ X, Iso.refl X, f, ?_, fun i hi ↦ by omega⟩
    show 𝟙 X ≫ 𝟙 X ≫ f = f
    simp
  | succ n ih =>
    obtain ⟨Z, a, b, ha, hb, rfl⟩ := hf
    obtain ⟨F, e, g, hfg, hF⟩ := ih hb
    refine ⟨F.precomp (a ≫ e.hom), Iso.refl X, g, ?_, ?_⟩
    · simp only [Iso.refl_hom, Category.id_comp, precomp_hom, Category.assoc, hfg]
    · intro i hi j
      cases i with
      | zero =>
        show (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C j).map (a ≫ e.hom) = 0
        simp only [Functor.map_comp, ha j, zero_comp]
      | succ i => exact hF i (by omega) j

private lemma homology_map_ext_one (M N : C) [HasExt.{w} C] (e : Ext M N 1) (i : ℤ) :
    (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C i).map e.hom = 0 := by
  by_cases hi : i = 0
  · subst i
    have := DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.isLE_shift
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor C 0).obj N) 0 1 (-1) (by omega)
    exact (DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isLE _ (-1) 0 (by omega)).eq_zero_of_tgt _
  · rcases lt_or_gt_of_ne hi with hi | hi
    · exact (DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isGE _ 0 i hi).eq_zero_of_src _
    · exact (DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isLE _ 0 i hi).eq_zero_of_src _

private lemma isGhostComposite_ext [HasExt.{w} C] [EnoughProjectives C]
    {M N : C} {n : ℕ} (e : Ext M N n) : IsGhostComposite n e.hom := by
  induction n generalizing M N with
  | zero => trivial
  | succ n ih =>
    let S := ShortComplex.mk _ _ (kernel.condition (Projective.π M))
    have hS : S.ShortExact :=
      { exact := ShortComplex.exact_of_f_is_kernel _ (kernelIsKernel S.g) }
    obtain ⟨e', rfl⟩ := Ext.contravariant_sequence_exact₃ hS N e
      (Ext.eq_zero_of_projective _) (by omega : 1 + n = n + 1)
    rw [Ext.comp_hom]
    refine ⟨_, hS.extClass.hom, _, homology_map_ext_one _ _ _, ?_, rfl⟩
    exact ((ih e').shift 1).postcomp _

end Ghosts

section Modules

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R]

private lemma single_mem_triangEnvelope_of_finite_free (M : ModuleCat.{u} R)
    [Module.Free R M] [Module.Finite R M] :
    (ObjectProperty.singleton
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of R R))).triangEnvelope
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj M) := by
  let S := DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0
  let P := (ObjectProperty.singleton (S.obj (ModuleCat.of R R))).triangEnvelope
  rcases subsingleton_or_nontrivial R with hR | hR
  · have : Subsingleton M := Module.subsingleton R M
    exact P.prop_of_isZero (S.map_isZero (ModuleCat.isZero_iff_subsingleton.mpr inferInstance))
  let f := fun _ : Fin (Module.finrank R M) ↦ ModuleCat.of R R
  let e : M ≅ ∏ᶜ f :=
    (Module.finBasis R M).equivFun.toModuleIso ≪≫ (ModuleCat.piIsoPi f).symm
  apply P.prop_of_iso (S.mapIso e).symm
  apply P.prop_of_iso (PreservesProduct.iso S f).symm
  exact P.prop_product fun _ ↦
    (ObjectProperty.singleton _).le_triangEnvelope _ ((ObjectProperty.singleton_iff _ _).2 rfl)

private lemma exists_trW_single_shift [IsNoetherianRing R] (M : ModuleCat.{u} R)
    [Module.Finite R M] (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ (N : ModuleCat.{u} R) (_ : Module.Finite R N)
      (f : (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj M ⟶
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj N)⟦(n : ℤ)⟧),
      (ObjectProperty.singleton
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj
          (ModuleCat.of R R))).triangEnvelope.trW f := by
  let D := DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)
  let S := DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0
  let P := (ObjectProperty.singleton (S.obj (ModuleCat.of R R))).triangEnvelope
  induction n generalizing M with
  | zero =>
    exact ⟨M, inferInstance, (shiftFunctorZero D ℤ).inv.app (S.obj M),
      P.trW_of_isIso _⟩
  | succ n ih =>
    obtain ⟨V, _, _, _, _, q, hq⟩ := Module.exists_finite_presentation R M
    let T := q.shortComplexKer
    have hT : T.ShortExact := LinearMap.shortExact_shortComplexKer hq
    obtain ⟨N, hN, f, hf⟩ := ih T.X₁
    have hδ : P.trW hT.singleδ :=
      ObjectProperty.trW.mk' P (rot_of_distTriang _ hT.singleTriangle_distinguished)
        (single_mem_triangEnvelope_of_finite_free T.X₂)
    let e := (shiftFunctorAdd' D (n : ℤ) 1 (↑(n + 1)) (by omega)).symm
    refine ⟨N, hN, hT.singleδ ≫ f⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧' ≫ e.hom.app (S.obj N), ?_⟩
    exact P.trW.comp_mem _ _ hδ
      (P.trW.comp_mem _ _ (hf.shift 1) (P.trW_of_isIso _))

private lemma ghostComposite_eq_zero_of_mem_triangEnvelopeIter
    {n : ℕ} {X Y : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)} {f : X ⟶ Y}
    (hf : IsGhostComposite (n + 1) f)
    (hX : (ObjectProperty.singleton
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R R))).triangEnvelopeIter n X) : f = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨F, e, g, hfg, hF⟩ := hf.exists_composableArrows
  have hFleft := (ObjectProperty.singleton
    ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj
      (ModuleCat.of R R))).triangEnvelopeIter n |>.prop_of_iso e hX
  have hz := comp_eq_zero_of_mem_triangEnvelopeIter
    (n + 1) (by omega) F (by simpa only [Nat.add_sub_cancel] using hFleft) hF
  rw [← hfg, hz, zero_comp, comp_zero]

private lemma hasProjectiveDimensionLT_of_triangEnvelopeIter_eq [IsNoetherianRing R]
    {n : ℕ}
    (h : (ObjectProperty.singleton
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R R))).triangEnvelopeIter n =
      (ObjectProperty.singleton
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj
          (ModuleCat.of R R))).triangEnvelope)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) [Module.Finite R M] : HasProjectiveDimensionLT M (n + 1) := by
  let S := DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0
  let P := (ObjectProperty.singleton (S.obj (ModuleCat.of R R))).triangEnvelope
  apply ModuleCat.hasProjectiveDimensionLT_of_forall_finite
  intro N _
  refine subsingleton_of_forall_eq 0 fun e ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨K, _, s, hs⟩ := exists_trW_single_shift M (n + 2)
  obtain ⟨A, a, b, hT, hA⟩ := (P.trW_iff' s).mp hs
  have ha : a ≫ e.hom = 0 := ghostComposite_eq_zero_of_mem_triangEnvelopeIter
    ((isGhostComposite_ext e).precomp a) (by rw [h]; exact hA)
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := (Triangle.mk a s b).yoneda_exact₂ hT e.hom ha
  have hle := DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.isLE_shift (S.obj K) 0 (↑(n + 2))
    (-(↑(n + 2))) (by omega)
  have hge := DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.isGE_shift (S.obj N) 0 (↑(n + 1))
    (-(↑(n + 1))) (by omega)
  have hgzero := DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.zero_of_isLE_of_isGE g
    (-(↑(n + 2))) (-(↑(n + 1))) (by omega) hle hge
  apply Ext.ext
  rw [Ext.zero_hom, hg, hgzero, comp_zero]

/-- **Stacks 0FXI**.
A Noetherian ring for which `R` strongly generates its perfect derived category — that is, for
which a single stage `⟨R⟩ₙ` already exhausts `⟨R⟩` — is regular and has finite Krull dimension. -/
@[stacks 0FXI]
theorem isRegularRing_and_ringKrullDim_ne_top_of_isStrongGenerator
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (h : ∃ n : ℕ,
      ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter
        (ObjectProperty.singleton
          ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of R R))) n =
      ObjectProperty.triangEnvelope
        (ObjectProperty.singleton
          ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of R R)))) :
    IsRegularRing R ∧ ringKrullDim R ≠ ⊤ := by
  rcases subsingleton_or_nontrivial R with hR | hR
  · refine ⟨isRegularRing_iff.mpr ?_, ?_⟩
    · intro p hp
      exact (hp.ne_top (Subsingleton.elim p ⊤)).elim
    · rw [ringKrullDim_eq_bot_iff_subsingleton.mpr hR]
      exact bot_ne_top
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := h
  have hd : (⨆ M : ModuleCat.{u} R, projectiveDimension M) < (n + 1 : ℕ) :=
    ((Stacks.GlobalDimension.CyclicModules.solution R (n + 1)).out 3 1).mp
      (fun M hM ↦ @hasProjectiveDimensionLT_of_triangEnvelopeIter_eq R _ _ n hn M hM)
  have hd₀ : (0 : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ ⨆ M : ModuleCat.{u} R, projectiveDimension M := by
    simpa only [ModuleCat.projectiveDimension_eq_zero_of_projective (ModuleCat.of R R)] using
      (le_iSup (fun M : ModuleCat.{u} R ↦ projectiveDimension M) (ModuleCat.of R R))
  generalize heq : (⨆ M : ModuleCat.{u} R, projectiveDimension M) = d at hd hd₀
  induction d with
  | bot => exact (not_le_of_gt (WithBot.bot_lt_coe (0 : ℕ∞)) hd₀).elim
  | coe d =>
    induction d with
    | top => exact (not_lt_of_ge le_top hd).elim
    | coe k =>
      have hk := ((Stacks.RegularRing.GlobalDimension.solution (R := R) k).out 1 2).mp heq
      refine ⟨hk.1, ?_⟩
      rw [hk.2]
      rw [← WithBot.coe_natCast, ne_eq, ← WithBot.coe_top, WithBot.coe_inj]
      exact ENat.natCast_ne_top k

end Modules

/-! ## Vanishing and splitting over a regular ring of finite dimension -/

section Regular

open CategoryTheory.Triangulated

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R]

/-- In a distinguished triangle whose third object has cohomology concentrated in degrees `≥ b`,
the first morphism is an isomorphism on cohomology in every degree `< b`. -/
private lemma isIso_homology_map_of_isGE
    {C : Type*} [Category C] [Abelian C] [HasDerivedCategory C]
    {A B D : DerivedCategory C} (u : A ⟶ B) (v : B ⟶ D) (w : D ⟶ A⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧)
    (hT : Triangle.mk u v w ∈ distTriang _) (i b : ℤ) (hi : i < b) [D.IsGE b] :
    IsIso ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C i).map u) := by
  have h₁ := DerivedCategory.HomologySequence.mono_homologyMap_mor₁_iff
    (Triangle.mk u v w) hT (i - 1) i (by omega)
  have h₂ := DerivedCategory.HomologySequence.epi_homologyMap_mor₁_iff
    (Triangle.mk u v w) hT i
  dsimp at h₁ h₂
  have : Mono ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C i).map u) := by
    rw [h₁]
    exact (DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isGE D b (i - 1) (by omega)).eq_of_src _ _
  have : Epi ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C i).map u) := by
    rw [h₂]
    exact (DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isGE D b i hi).eq_of_tgt _ _
  exact isIso_of_mono_of_epi _

/-- In a distinguished triangle whose first object has cohomology concentrated in degrees `≤ a`,
the second morphism is an isomorphism on cohomology in every degree `> a`. -/
private lemma isIso_homology_map_of_isLE
    {C : Type*} [Category C] [Abelian C] [HasDerivedCategory C]
    {A B D : DerivedCategory C} (u : A ⟶ B) (v : B ⟶ D) (w : D ⟶ A⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧)
    (hT : Triangle.mk u v w ∈ distTriang _) (i a : ℤ) (hi : a < i) [A.IsLE a] :
    IsIso ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C i).map v) := by
  have h₁ := DerivedCategory.HomologySequence.mono_homologyMap_mor₂_iff
    (Triangle.mk u v w) hT i
  have h₂ := DerivedCategory.HomologySequence.epi_homologyMap_mor₂_iff
    (Triangle.mk u v w) hT i (i + 1) (by omega)
  dsimp at h₁ h₂
  have : Mono ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C i).map v) := by
    rw [h₁]
    exact (DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isLE A a i hi).eq_of_src _ _
  have : Epi ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C i).map v) := by
    rw [h₂]
    exact (DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isLE A a (i + 1) (by omega)).eq_of_tgt _ _
  exact isIso_of_mono_of_epi _

/-- Over a regular ring of Krull dimension `d`, every module has projective dimension at most
`d`, because `d` is the global dimension. -/
private lemma globalDimension_modules [IsRegularRing R]
    (d : ℕ) (hdim : ringKrullDim R = d) (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) :
    HasProjectiveDimensionLE M d := by
  rw [← projectiveDimension_le_iff]
  have hglobal : (⨆ N : ModuleCat.{u} R, projectiveDimension N) =
      (d : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
    ((Stacks.RegularRing.GlobalDimension.solution d).out 1 2).mpr
      (show IsRegularRing R ∧ ringKrullDim R = (d : WithBot ℕ∞) from
        And.intro inferInstance (by simpa using hdim))
  exact (le_iSup (fun N : ModuleCat.{u} R ↦ projectiveDimension N) M).trans hglobal.le

/-- Over a regular ring of Krull dimension `d`, a morphism from a module placed in degree `m` to
an object with cohomology in degrees `≤ b` vanishes as soon as `b < m - d`: resolve the module by
a projective complex of length `d` and use that there is no nonzero morphism from a K-projective
complex concentrated in degrees `≥ m - d` into a complex concentrated in degrees `≤ b`. -/
private lemma single_hom_eq_zero [IsRegularRing R]
    (d : ℕ) (hdim : ringKrullDim R = d) (M : ModuleCat.{u} R)
    (m b : ℤ) (hmb : b < m - d) (Y : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R))
    [Y.IsLE b] (f : (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat R) m).obj M ⟶ Y) : f = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨F, hF⟩ :=
    ((CategoryTheory.hasProjectiveDimensionLE_tfae_leftResolution M d).out 1 2).mp
      (globalDimension_modules d hdim M)
  let E : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℤ :=
    F.complex.extend ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat
  have singleIso : (((ChainComplex.single₀ (ModuleCat.{u} R)).obj M).extend
      ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat) ≅
      (CochainComplex.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj M :=
    HomologicalComplex.extendSingleIso ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat M 0 0 rfl
  let α : E ⟶ (CochainComplex.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj M :=
    HomologicalComplex.extendMap F.π ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat ≫ singleIso.hom
  have hE (i : ℤ) (hi : i ≤ 0) : E.X i ≅ F.complex.X i.natAbs := by
    apply HomologicalComplex.extendXIso _ ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat (i := i.natAbs)
    rw [show ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat.f i.natAbs = -(i.natAbs : ℤ) from rfl]
    omega
  have hpos (i : ℤ) (hi : 0 < i) : IsZero (E.X i) := by
    apply HomologicalComplex.isZero_extend_X
    intro n
    rw [show ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat.f n = -(n : ℤ) from rfl]
    omega
  have hproj (i : ℤ) : Projective (E.X i) := by
    by_cases hi : i ≤ 0
    · exact Projective.of_iso (hE i hi).symm (F.property i.natAbs)
    · exact (hpos i (by omega)).projective
  have hge : E.IsStrictlyGE (-(d : ℤ)) := by
    rw [CochainComplex.isStrictlyGE_iff]
    intro i hi
    by_cases hnonpos : i ≤ 0
    · exact IsZero.of_iso (hF i.natAbs (by omega)) (hE i hnonpos)
    · exact hpos i (by omega)
  have hle : E.IsStrictlyLE 0 := by
    rw [CochainComplex.isStrictlyLE_iff]
    exact fun i hi => hpos i hi
  have hα : QuasiIso α := by
    dsimp [α]
    infer_instance
  let P := (shiftFunctor (CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℤ) (-m)).obj E
  let αm : P ⟶ (CochainComplex.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) m).obj M :=
    (shiftFunctor (CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℤ) (-m)).map α ≫
      ((CochainComplex.singleFunctors (ModuleCat.{u} R)).shiftIso (-m) m 0 (by omega)).hom.app M
  let (i : ℤ) : Projective (P.X i) := by
    apply Projective.of_iso
      (CochainComplex.shiftFunctorObjXIso E (-m) i (i - m) (by omega)).symm
    exact hproj (i - m)
  let : P.IsStrictlyGE (m - d) := E.isStrictlyGE_shift (-(d : ℤ)) (-m) (m - d) (by omega)
  let : P.IsStrictlyLE m := E.isStrictlyLE_shift 0 (-m) m (by omega)
  let : P.IsKProjective := CochainComplex.isKProjective_of_projective P m
  have hαm : QuasiIso αm := by
    dsimp [αm]
    infer_instance
  obtain ⟨L, _, ⟨eL⟩⟩ := DerivedCategory.exists_iso_Q_obj_of_isLE Y b
  let eM : (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat R) m).obj M ≅
      DerivedCategory.Q.obj P :=
    (DerivedCategory.singleFunctorIsoCompQ (ModuleCat R) m).app M ≪≫
      (asIso (DerivedCategory.Q.map αm)).symm
  apply (cancel_epi eM.inv).1
  apply (cancel_mono eL.hom).1
  have hz := (CochainComplex.IsKProjective.hom_eq_zero_of_isStrictlyGE_of_isLE
    P L (m - d) b hmb).2 (eM.inv ≫ f ≫ eL.hom)
  simp [hz]

/-- Over a regular ring of Krull dimension `d`, a morphism from a bounded object with cohomology
in degrees `≥ a` to an object with cohomology in degrees `≤ c` vanishes as soon as `c < a - d`:
induct on the width of the source using its truncation triangles. -/
private lemma bounded_hom_eq_zero [IsRegularRing R]
    (d : ℕ) (hdim : ringKrullDim R = d)
    (X Y : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)) (a b c : ℤ)
    [X.IsGE a] [X.IsLE b] [Y.IsLE c] (hc : c < a - d) (f : X ⟶ Y) : f = 0 := by
  have single : ∀ (m : ℤ) (Z : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)) [Z.IsGE m] [Z.IsLE m],
      c < m - d → ∀ g : Z ⟶ Y, g = 0 := by
    intro m Z _ _ hcm g
    obtain ⟨M, ⟨e⟩⟩ := DerivedCategory.exists_iso_singleFunctor_obj_of_isGE_of_isLE Z m
    apply (cancel_epi e.inv).1
    simpa using single_hom_eq_zero d hdim M m c hcm Y (e.inv ≫ g)
  have aux : ∀ (n : ℕ) (a b : ℤ) (X : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)),
      c < a - d → b ≤ a + n → ∀ [X.IsGE a] [X.IsLE b],
        ∀ (f : X ⟶ Y), f = 0 := by
    intro n
    induction n with
    | zero =>
        intro a b X hca hab hge hle f
        rcases lt_or_ge b a with hba | hba
        · exact (DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.isZero X b a hba).eq_of_src _ _
        · obtain rfl : a = b := by omega
          exact single a X hca f
    | succ n ih =>
        intro a b X hca hab hge hle f
        rcases lt_or_ge b a with hba | hba
        · exact (DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.isZero X b a hba).eq_of_src _ _
        · let T := (DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.triangleLTGE b).obj X
          let : X.IsGE a := hge
          let : X.IsLE b := hle
          have hT : T ∈ distTriang _ :=
            DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.triangleLTGE_distinguished b X
          let : T.obj₁.IsGE a := by
            rw [DerivedCategory.isGE_iff]
            intro i hi
            let hIso : IsIso
                ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat R) i).map T.mor₁) := by
              apply isIso_homology_map_of_isGE T.mor₁ T.mor₂ T.mor₃ hT i b
              omega
            exact (DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isGE X a i hi).of_iso
              (@asIso _ _ _ _ _ hIso)
          let : T.obj₃.IsLE b := by
            rw [DerivedCategory.isLE_iff]
            intro i hi
            let hIso : IsIso
                ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat R) i).map T.mor₂) := by
              apply isIso_homology_map_of_isLE T.mor₁ T.mor₂ T.mor₃ hT i (b - 1)
              omega
            exact (DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isLE X b i hi).of_iso
              (@asIso _ _ _ _ _ hIso).symm
          have hf₁ : T.mor₁ ≫ f = 0 := by
            apply ih a (b - 1) T.obj₁ hca (by omega)
          obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := T.yoneda_exact₂ hT f hf₁
          have hg0 : g = 0 := single b T.obj₃ (by omega) g
          dsimp [T] at hg
          exact hg.trans (hg0 ▸ comp_zero)
  exact aux (b - a).toNat a b X hc (by omega) f

/-- **Stacks 0FXJ**.
Let `R` be a regular Noetherian ring of finite dimension `d`. If `K` and `L` are bounded-above
derived `R`-modules, the cohomology of `K` vanishes in degrees at most `k`, and the cohomology of
`L` vanishes in degrees at least `k - d + 1`, then every morphism from `K` to `L` is zero. -/
@[stacks 0FXJ]
theorem subsingleton_hom_of_isGE_of_isLE [IsRegularRing R]
    (d : ℕ) (hdim : ringKrullDim R = d)
    (K L : DerivedCategory.Minus (ModuleCat.{u} R)) (k : ℤ)
    (hK : K.obj.IsGE (k + 1)) (hL : L.obj.IsLE (k - d)) :
    Subsingleton (K.obj ⟶ L.obj) := by
  let : K.obj.IsGE (k + 1) := hK
  let : L.obj.IsLE (k - d) := hL
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := K.property
  let : K.obj.IsLE b := hb
  exact ⟨fun f g => sub_eq_zero.mp
    (bounded_hom_eq_zero d hdim K.obj L.obj (k + 1) b (k - d) (by omega) (f - g))⟩

/-- **Stacks 0FXK**.
Let `R` be a regular Noetherian ring of finite positive dimension `d`. If a perfect derived
`R`-module `K` has zero cohomology in every degree from `k - d + 2` through `k`, then `K` is
isomorphic to the biproduct of its truncations in degrees at most `k - d + 1` and at least
`k + 1`. -/
@[stacks 0FXK]
theorem iso_biproduct_truncations_of_cohomology_isZero [IsRegularRing R]
    (d : ℕ) (hdim : ringKrullDim R = d) (hd : 1 ≤ d)
    (K : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)) (hKperfect : StacksDraft.Perfect.IsPerfect K) (k : ℤ)
    (hK : ∀ i : ℤ, k - d + 2 ≤ i → i ≤ k →
      IsZero ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).obj K)) :
    Nonempty
      (K ≅
        (DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.truncLE (k - d + 1)).obj K ⊞
          (DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.truncGE (k + 1)).obj K) := by
  let t := DerivedCategory.TStructure.t (C := ModuleCat.{u} R)
  let a : ℤ := k - d + 1
  let b : ℤ := k + 1
  let A := (t.truncLE a).obj K
  let G := (t.truncGE (a + 1)).obj K
  let T := (t.triangleLEGE a (a + 1) rfl).obj K
  have hT : T ∈ distTriang _ := t.triangleLEGE_distinguished a (a + 1) rfl K
  have hGge : t.IsGE G b := by
    apply (DerivedCategory.isGE_iff G b).2
    intro i hi
    by_cases hi' : i < a + 1
    · exact DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isGE G (a + 1) i hi'
    · have hKi : IsZero ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).obj K) :=
        hK i (by dsimp [a] at hi' ⊢; omega) (by dsimp [b] at hi ⊢; omega)
      have hAi : IsZero
          ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) (i + 1)).obj A) :=
        DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isLE A a (i + 1) (by omega)
      exact ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).homologySequence_exact₃
        T hT i (i + 1) rfl).isZero_of_both_isZero hKi hAi
  obtain ⟨P, p, q, hPge, hPle, hPfinite, hPprojective, ⟨eK⟩⟩ := hKperfect
  have hKle : t.IsLE K q := ⟨P, eK, hPle⟩
  let Gm : DerivedCategory.Minus (ModuleCat.{u} R) :=
    ⟨G, q, inferInstance⟩
  let Am : DerivedCategory.Minus (ModuleCat.{u} R) :=
    ⟨A⟦1⟧, q - 1, t.isLE_shift A q 1 (q - 1) (by omega)⟩
  have hAle : Am.obj.IsLE (k - d) := by
    dsimp [Am]
    exact t.isLE_shift A a 1 (k - d) (by dsimp [a]; omega)
  have hzero : T.mor₃ = 0 := by
    show (t.truncGEδLE a (a + 1) rfl).app K = 0
    have hs := subsingleton_hom_of_isGE_of_isLE d hdim Gm Am k hGge hAle
    apply @Subsingleton.elim _ hs
  obtain ⟨e₁, -⟩ := Pretriangulated.exists_iso_binaryBiproduct_of_distTriang T hT hzero
  change K ≅ A ⊞ G at e₁
  have : IsIso ((t.truncGE b).map ((t.truncGEπ (a + 1)).app K)) :=
    t.isIso_truncGE_map_truncGEπ_app b (a + 1) (by dsimp [a, b]; omega) K
  have : IsIso ((t.truncGEπ b).app G) :=
    (t.isGE_iff_isIso_truncGEπ_app b G).1 hGge
  let eG : G ≅ (t.truncGE b).obj K :=
    asIso ((t.truncGEπ b).app G) ≪≫
      (asIso ((t.truncGE b).map ((t.truncGEπ (a + 1)).app K))).symm
  show Nonempty (K ≅ A ⊞ (t.truncGE b).obj K)
  exact ⟨e₁ ≪≫ Limits.biprod.mapIso (Iso.refl A) eG⟩

end Regular

/-! ## Regular rings of finite dimension strongly generate -/

section RegularStronglyGenerates

/-- The retract closure of a property closed under binary products is again closed under binary
products: a retract of `X` and a retract of `Y` assemble into a retract of `X ⨯ Y`. -/
private lemma isClosedUnderBinaryProducts_retractClosure
    {C : Type*} [Category* C] [HasBinaryProducts C]
    (P : ObjectProperty C) [P.IsClosedUnderBinaryProducts] :
    P.retractClosure.IsClosedUnderBinaryProducts := by
  refine .mk' ?_
  rintro _ ⟨F, hF⟩
  obtain ⟨X, hX, ⟨rX⟩⟩ := hF ⟨.left⟩
  obtain ⟨Y, hY, ⟨rY⟩⟩ := hF ⟨.right⟩
  apply P.retractClosure.prop_of_iso (HasLimit.isoOfNatIso (diagramIsoPair F)).symm
  exact ⟨X ⨯ Y, P.prop_prod _ _ hX hY,
    ⟨{ i := Limits.prod.map rX.i rY.i
       r := Limits.prod.map rX.r rY.r
       retract := by rw [Limits.prod.map_map, rX.retract, rY.retract,
         Limits.prod.map_id_id] }⟩⟩

/-- The zeroth stage `⟨G⟩₁` of a triangulated envelope is closed under finite products, being the
retract closure of the binary-product closure of the shifts of `G`. -/
private lemma isClosedUnderFiniteProducts_triangEnvelopeIter_zero
    {C : Type*} [Category C] [HasZeroObject C] [HasShift C ℤ] [Preadditive C]
    [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor C n).Additive] [Pretriangulated C]
    (G : C) : ((ObjectProperty.singleton G).triangEnvelopeIter 0).IsClosedUnderFiniteProducts := by
  rw [ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter_zero]
  have := isClosedUnderBinaryProducts_retractClosure
    ((ObjectProperty.singleton G).shiftClosure ℤ).binaryProductsClosure
  let P := ((ObjectProperty.singleton G).shiftClosure ℤ).binaryProductsClosure.retractClosure
  have hG : P G := by
    simpa only [ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter_zero] using
      (ObjectProperty.singleton G).le_triangEnvelopeIter 0 G
        ((ObjectProperty.singleton_iff G G).2 rfl)
  have : P.Nonempty := ObjectProperty.nonempty_of_prop hG
  exact ObjectProperty.IsClosedUnderFiniteProducts.mk'

/-- A finite biproduct of objects of `⟨G⟩₁` again lies in `⟨G⟩₁`. -/
private lemma triangEnvelopeIter_zero_biproduct
    {C : Type*} [Category C] [HasZeroObject C] [HasShift C ℤ] [Preadditive C]
    [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor C n).Additive] [Pretriangulated C]
    (G : C) {J : Type*} [Finite J] (F : J → C) [HasBiproduct F]
    (hF : ∀ j, (ObjectProperty.singleton G).triangEnvelopeIter 0 (F j)) :
    (ObjectProperty.singleton G).triangEnvelopeIter 0 (⨁ F) := by
  have := isClosedUnderFiniteProducts_triangEnvelopeIter_zero G
  exact ObjectProperty.prop_of_isLimit_fan _ (biproduct.isLimit F) hF

/-- A finite projective module placed in any degree lies in the zeroth stage `⟨R[0]⟩₁`: it is a
retract of a finite free module, and a finite free module in degree `n` is a biproduct of shifts
of `R[0]`. -/
private lemma triangEnvelopeIter_zero_single_of_finite_of_projective
    {R : Type u} [Ring R] (M : ModuleCat.{u} R)
    [Module.Finite R M] [Projective M] (n : ℤ) :
    (ObjectProperty.singleton
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R R))).triangEnvelopeIter 0
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj M) := by
  let S := DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) n
  let G := (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of R R)
  let P := (ObjectProperty.singleton G).triangEnvelopeIter 0
  have := isClosedUnderFiniteProducts_triangEnvelopeIter_zero G
  have hR : P (S.obj (ModuleCat.of R R)) := by
    have hG : P G := (ObjectProperty.singleton G).le_triangEnvelopeIter 0 G
      ((ObjectProperty.singleton_iff G G).2 rfl)
    exact P.prop_of_iso
      (((DerivedCategory.singleFunctors (ModuleCat.{u} R)).shiftIso (-n) n 0 (by omega)).app
        (ModuleCat.of R R)) (P.le_shift (-n) G hG)
  obtain ⟨m, f, hf⟩ := Module.Finite.exists_fin' R M
  let f' : ModuleCat.of R (Fin m → R) ⟶ M := ModuleCat.ofHom f
  have : Epi f' := (ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective f').mpr hf
  let r : Retract M (ModuleCat.of R (Fin m → R)) :=
    { i := Projective.factorThru (𝟙 M) f'
      r := f'
      retract := Projective.factorThru_comp _ _ }
  apply P.prop_of_retract (r.map S)
  let F : Fin m → ModuleCat.{u} R := fun _ => ModuleCat.of R R
  let e : (⨁ F) ≅ ModuleCat.of R (Fin m → R) :=
    (biproduct.isoProduct F) ≪≫ ModuleCat.piIsoPi F
  apply P.prop_of_iso (S.mapIso e)
  apply P.prop_of_iso (S.mapBiproduct F).symm
  exact triangEnvelopeIter_zero_biproduct G _ (fun _ => hR)

/-- A projective object surjecting onto the degree-`n` homology of a cochain complex is the source
of a chain map from the complex it spans in degree `n` which is epi on degree-`n` homology. -/
private lemma exists_hom_from_single_epi_homology
    {C : Type*} [Category* C] [Abelian C]
    (P : CochainComplex C ℤ) (M : C) [Projective M] (n : ℤ)
    (f : M ⟶ P.homology n) [Epi f] :
    ∃ g : (HomologicalComplex.single C (.up ℤ) n).obj M ⟶ P,
      Epi (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap g n) := by
  let l := Projective.factorThru f (P.homologyπ n)
  let g := HomologicalComplex.mkHomFromSingle (l ≫ P.iCycles n)
    (fun k hk => by simp)
  have hc : HomologicalComplex.cyclesMap g n =
      (HomologicalComplex.singleObjCyclesSelfIso (.up ℤ) n M).hom ≫ l := by
    apply (cancel_mono (P.iCycles n)).mp
    simp [g, HomologicalComplex.singleObjCyclesSelfIso_hom]
  have hh : HomologicalComplex.homologyMap g n =
      (HomologicalComplex.singleObjHomologySelfIso (.up ℤ) n M).hom ≫ f := by
    apply (cancel_epi (((HomologicalComplex.single C (.up ℤ) n).obj M).homologyπ n)).mp
    simp [hc, Category.assoc, l]
  exact ⟨g, hh ▸ inferInstance⟩

/-- The derived-category form of the previous lemma: a projective object surjecting onto the
degree-`n` cohomology of `K` is the source of a morphism in `D(C)` out of it placed in degree `n`
which is epi on degree-`n` cohomology. -/
private lemma exists_hom_single_epi_homology
    {C : Type*} [Category* C] [Abelian C]
    (K : DerivedCategory C) (M : C) [Projective M] (n : ℤ)
    (f : M ⟶ (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C n).obj K) [Epi f] :
    ∃ g : (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor C n).obj M ⟶ K,
      Epi ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C n).map g) := by
  let P := DerivedCategory.Q.objPreimage K
  let e := DerivedCategory.Q.objObjPreimageIso K
  let H := DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C n
  let eH := (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctorFactors C n).app P
  let f' : M ⟶ P.homology n := f ≫ H.map e.inv ≫ eH.hom
  have he : IsIso (H.map e.inv) := by dsimp [H, e]; infer_instance
  have heH : IsIso eH.hom := by dsimp [eH]; infer_instance
  have : Epi f' := epi_comp f (H.map e.inv ≫ eH.hom)
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_hom_from_single_epi_homology P M n f'
  have hcomp : Epi ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctorFactors C n).hom.app _ ≫
      HomologicalComplex.homologyMap g n) :=
    epi_comp' inferInstance hg
  have : Epi (H.map (DerivedCategory.Q.map g)) :=
    (epi_comp_iff_of_isIso _ eH.hom).mp (by
      show Epi ((DerivedCategory.Q ⋙ DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C n).map g ≫
        (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctorFactors C n).hom.app P)
      rw [(DerivedCategory.homologyFunctorFactors C n).hom.naturality g]
      exact hcomp)
  refine ⟨DerivedCategory.Q.map g ≫ e.hom, ?_⟩
  rw [H.map_comp]
  infer_instance

/-- Every cohomology object of a projective object placed in a single degree is projective: it is
either zero or the object itself. -/
private lemma projective_homology_single
    {C : Type*} [Category* C] [Abelian C] (M : C) [Projective M] (n i : ℤ) :
    Projective ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor C i).obj
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor C n).obj M)) := by
  rcases lt_trichotomy i n with h | rfl | h
  · exact (DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isGE _ n i h).projective
  · exact Projective.of_iso
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctorCompHomologyFunctorIso C i).app M).symm inferInstance
  · exact (DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isLE _ n i h).projective

/-- A bounded object of `D(R)` with finite cohomology modules admits a morphism onto it from an
object of the zeroth stage `⟨R[0]⟩₁` which is surjective on cohomology in every degree and has
projective cohomology: take the biproduct, over the degrees in the bounded range, of finite free
modules covering the cohomology there. -/
private lemma exists_finite_projective_homology_cover
    {R : Type u} [Ring R] (K : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)) (a b : ℤ)
    [K.IsGE a] [K.IsLE b]
    (hfin : ∀ i : ℤ, Module.Finite R
      ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).obj K)) :
    ∃ (F : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)) (f : F ⟶ K),
      (ObjectProperty.singleton
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj
          (ModuleCat.of R R))).triangEnvelopeIter 0 F ∧
      (∀ i, Epi ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).map f)) ∧
      (∀ i, Projective ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).obj F)) := by
  classical
  let H := DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R)
  have hcover (i : Finset.Icc a b) :
      ∃ (M : ModuleCat.{u} R), Module.Finite R M ∧ Projective M ∧
        ∃ f : (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i.1).obj M ⟶ K,
          Epi ((H i.1).map f) := by
    have := hfin i.1
    obtain ⟨m, p, hp⟩ := Module.Finite.exists_fin' R ((H i.1).obj K)
    let M := ModuleCat.of R (Fin m → R)
    have : Projective M := ModuleCat.projective_of_categoryTheory_projective M
    let p' : M ⟶ (H i.1).obj K := ModuleCat.ofHom p
    have : Epi p' := (ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective _).mpr hp
    obtain ⟨f, hf⟩ := exists_hom_single_epi_homology K M i.1 p'
    exact ⟨M, inferInstance, inferInstance, f, hf⟩
  choose M hMfin hMproj f hf using hcover
  let F : Finset.Icc a b → DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R) := fun i =>
    (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i.1).obj (M i)
  let φ : (⨁ F) ⟶ K := biproduct.desc f
  refine ⟨⨁ F, φ, triangEnvelopeIter_zero_biproduct _ F (fun i => ?_), ?_, ?_⟩
  · have := hMfin i
    have := hMproj i
    exact triangEnvelopeIter_zero_single_of_finite_of_projective (M i) i.1
  · intro i
    by_cases hi : i ∈ Finset.Icc a b
    · have := hf ⟨i, hi⟩
      apply epi_of_epi_fac (f := (H i).map (biproduct.ι F ⟨i, hi⟩))
        (h := (H i).map (f ⟨i, hi⟩))
      show (H i).map (biproduct.ι F ⟨i, hi⟩) ≫ (H i).map φ = _
      simp only [← Functor.map_comp, φ, biproduct.ι_desc]
    · have hz : IsZero ((H i).obj K) := by
        simp only [Finset.mem_Icc, not_and_or, not_le] at hi
        rcases hi with hi | hi
        · exact DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isGE K a i hi
        · exact DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isLE K b i hi
      exact hz.epi _
  · intro i
    have hproj (j : Finset.Icc a b) : Projective ((H i).obj (F j)) := by
      have := hMproj j
      exact projective_homology_single (M j) j.1 i
    apply Projective.of_iso ((H i).mapBiproduct F).symm
    refine ⟨fun p q _ => ?_⟩
    refine ⟨biproduct.desc (fun j => ?_), ?_⟩
    · have : Projective (((H i).obj ∘ F) j) := hproj j
      exact Projective.factorThru (biproduct.ι _ j ≫ p) q
    · apply biproduct.hom_ext'
      intro j
      simp

/-- A perfect object over a Noetherian ring is bounded on both sides and has finite cohomology
modules, read off from a bounded representative by finite modules. -/
private lemma bounded_and_finite_homology_of_isPerfect
    {R : Type u} [Ring R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (K : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)) (hK : StacksDraft.Perfect.IsPerfect K) :
    (∃ a : ℤ, K.IsGE a) ∧ (∃ b : ℤ, K.IsLE b) ∧
      ∀ i : ℤ, Module.Finite R
        ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).obj K) := by
  obtain ⟨P, a, b, hPa, hPb, hPfin, _, ⟨e⟩⟩ := hK
  have := hPa
  have := hPb
  refine ⟨⟨a, ?_⟩, ⟨b, ?_⟩, fun i => ?_⟩
  · exact DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.isGE_of_iso e.symm a
  · exact DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.isLE_of_iso e.symm b
  · have := hPfin i
    have : Module.Finite R (P.cycles i) :=
      Module.Finite.of_injective (P.iCycles i).hom
        ((ModuleCat.mono_iff_injective _).mp inferInstance)
    have hfin : Module.Finite R (P.homology i) :=
      Module.Finite.of_surjective (P.homologyπ i).hom
        ((ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective _).mp inferInstance)
    have : Module.Finite R
        ((HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) (.up ℤ) i).obj P) := hfin
    let eH := ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctorFactors (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).app P).symm ≪≫
      (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).mapIso e.symm
    exact Module.Finite.equiv eH.toLinearEquiv

/-- A perfect object all of whose cohomology modules have projective dimension at most `d` lies in
the stage `⟨R[0]⟩_(d + 1)`. The induction on `d` covers the cohomology by a projective object of
the zeroth stage, completes to a distinguished triangle, and applies the inductive hypothesis to
the cone, whose cohomology has projective dimension one lower. -/
private lemma triangEnvelopeIter_of_isPerfect_of_hasProjectiveDimensionLE_homology
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] (d : ℕ)
    (K : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)) (hK : StacksDraft.Perfect.IsPerfect K)
    (hpd : ∀ i, HasProjectiveDimensionLE
      ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).obj K) d) :
    (ObjectProperty.singleton
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R R))).triangEnvelopeIter d K := by
  let G := (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of R R)
  let P := ObjectProperty.singleton G
  let H := DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R)
  have hperfect :
      (StacksDraft.Perfect.IsPerfect :
        ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R))) = P.triangEnvelope :=
    StacksDraft.Perfect.isPerfect_eq_triangEnvelope_singleton_regularModule
  induction d generalizing K with
  | zero =>
      obtain ⟨⟨a, ha⟩, ⟨b, hb⟩, hfin⟩ :=
        bounded_and_finite_homology_of_isPerfect K hK
      have := ha
      have := hb
      obtain ⟨e⟩ :=
        DerivedCategory.nonempty_iso_biproduct_singleFunctor_obj_homology_of_forall_ext_eq_zero
          K a b (fun i j p hij hp ξ => by
            have := hpd i
            exact ξ.eq_zero_of_hasProjectiveDimensionLT 1 (by omega))
      apply (P.triangEnvelopeIter 0).prop_of_iso e.symm
      apply triangEnvelopeIter_zero_biproduct G
      intro i
      have := hfin i.1
      have : Projective ((H i.1).obj K) :=
        (projective_iff_hasProjectiveDimensionLE_zero _).mpr (hpd i.1)
      exact triangEnvelopeIter_zero_single_of_finite_of_projective _ i.1
  | succ d ih =>
      obtain ⟨⟨a, ha⟩, ⟨b, hb⟩, hfin⟩ :=
        bounded_and_finite_homology_of_isPerfect K hK
      have := ha
      have := hb
      obtain ⟨F, f, hF, hf, hFproj⟩ := exists_finite_projective_homology_cover K a b hfin
      obtain ⟨L, g, δ, hT⟩ := distinguished_cocone_triangle₁ f
      let T := Triangle.mk g f δ
      have hL : StacksDraft.Perfect.IsPerfect L := by
        rw [hperfect]
        exact P.triangEnvelope.ext_of_isTriangulatedClosed₁ T hT
          (P.triangEnvelopeIter_le_triangEnvelope 0 F hF) (hperfect ▸ hK)
      have hLpd (i : ℤ) : HasProjectiveDimensionLE ((H i).obj L) d := by
        have hδ : DerivedCategory.HomologySequence.δ T (i - 1) i = 0 :=
          (DerivedCategory.HomologySequence.epi_homologyMap_mor₂_iff T hT (i - 1) i).mp
            (hf (i - 1))
        have hm : Mono ((H i).map g) :=
          (DerivedCategory.HomologySequence.mono_homologyMap_mor₁_iff T hT (i - 1) i).mpr hδ
        have he := hf i
        have hgf : g ≫ f = 0 := comp_distTriang_mor_zero₁₂ T hT
        let S := ShortComplex.mk ((H i).map g) ((H i).map f)
          (by rw [← Functor.map_comp, hgf, Functor.map_zero])
        have hS : S.ShortExact :=
          { exact := DerivedCategory.HomologySequence.exact₂ T hT i }
        have := hFproj i
        exact hS.hasProjectiveDimensionLT_X₁ (d + 1)
          (hasProjectiveDimensionLT_of_ge ((H i).obj F) 1 (d + 1) (by omega)) (hpd i)
      have hLi := ih L hL hLpd
      rw [ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter_succ, ← ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter_zero]
      apply ObjectProperty.le_retractClosure
      exact ⟨F, L⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧, f, δ, T.rotate.mor₃, rot_of_distTriang T hT,
        hF, (P.triangEnvelopeIter d).le_shift 1 L hLi⟩

/-- Over a regular ring of finite Krull dimension the projective dimensions of all modules are
bounded by a single natural number, namely the global dimension. The zero ring, whose Krull
dimension is `⊥`, is covered separately by the bound `0`. -/
private lemma exists_uniform_projectiveDimension_bound
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsRegularRing R] (hdim : ringKrullDim R ≠ ⊤) :
    ∃ d : ℕ, ∀ M : ModuleCat.{u} R, HasProjectiveDimensionLE M d := by
  by_cases hbot : ringKrullDim R = ⊥
  · have : Subsingleton R := ringKrullDim_eq_bot_iff_subsingleton.mp hbot
    refine ⟨0, fun M => ?_⟩
    have : Subsingleton M := Module.subsingleton R M
    have : Projective M := (ModuleCat.isZero_of_subsingleton M).projective
    infer_instance
  · obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := WithBot.ne_bot_iff_exists.mp hbot
    have hxfin : x ≠ ⊤ := by
      intro h
      apply hdim
      rw [← hx, h]
      rfl
    obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := ENat.ne_top_iff_exists.mp hxfin
    have hdimd : ringKrullDim R = (d : WithBot ℕ∞) := by rw [← hx, ← hd]; rfl
    exact ⟨d, globalDimension_modules d hdimd⟩

/-- **Stacks 0FXL**.
Over a regular ring of finite Krull dimension, the regular module placed in degree zero is a strong
generator of the perfect derived category: a single stage `⟨R⟩ₙ` of the triangulated envelope of
`R[0]` already contains every perfect complex. One may take for `n` the global dimension of `R`. -/
@[stacks 0FXL]
theorem exists_triangEnvelopeIter_eq_isPerfect_of_isRegularRing
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsRegularRing R] (hdim : ringKrullDim R ≠ ⊤) :
    ∃ n : ℕ,
      ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter
          (ObjectProperty.singleton
            ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of R R))) n =
        (StacksDraft.Perfect.IsPerfect :
          ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R))) := by
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := exists_uniform_projectiveDimension_bound hdim
  refine ⟨d, le_antisymm ?_ ?_⟩
  · rw [StacksDraft.Perfect.isPerfect_eq_triangEnvelope_singleton_regularModule]
    exact ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter_le_triangEnvelope _ d
  · intro K hK
    exact triangEnvelopeIter_of_isPerfect_of_hasProjectiveDimensionLE_homology d K hK
      (fun i => hd ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).obj K))

end RegularStronglyGenerates

/-! ## Regularity, strong generation, and the regular module -/

section StrongGeneratorCharacterization

/-- **Stacks 0FXM**.
For a Noetherian ring `R` the following are equivalent: `R` is regular of finite Krull dimension;
the perfect derived category of `R` admits a strong generator; and the regular module placed in
degree zero is such a strong generator. The implication from an arbitrary strong generator to the
regular module uses that any object of the perfect derived category already lies in some finite
stage of the envelope of `R[0]`, so the stages of its own envelope are absorbed into those of
`R[0]`. -/
@[stacks 0FXM]
theorem isRegularRing_and_ringKrullDim_ne_top_iff_hasStrongGenerator_iff_regularModule
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] :
    let D := DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)
    let perfect := (StacksDraft.Perfect.IsPerfect : ObjectProperty D)
    let regularModule :=
      (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of R R)
    let regularFinite := IsRegularRing R ∧ ringKrullDim R ≠ ⊤
    let hasStrongGenerator := ∃ E : D, ∃ n : ℕ,
      ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter (ObjectProperty.singleton E) n = perfect
    let regularModuleIsStrongGenerator := ∃ n : ℕ,
      ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter (ObjectProperty.singleton regularModule) n = perfect
    (regularFinite ↔ hasStrongGenerator) ∧
      (hasStrongGenerator ↔ regularModuleIsStrongGenerator) := by
  dsimp
  let R0 := (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of R R)
  let P := ObjectProperty.singleton R0
  let perfect :=
    (StacksDraft.Perfect.IsPerfect : ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)))
  have hclassical : perfect = P.triangEnvelope :=
    StacksDraft.Perfect.isPerfect_eq_triangEnvelope_singleton_regularModule
  have toRegular : (∃ E, ∃ n, (ObjectProperty.singleton E).triangEnvelopeIter n = perfect) →
      ∃ n, P.triangEnvelopeIter n = perfect := by
    rintro ⟨E, n, hn⟩
    have hE : P.triangEnvelope E := by
      rw [← hclassical, ← hn]
      exact (ObjectProperty.singleton E).le_triangEnvelopeIter n E
        ((ObjectProperty.singleton_iff E E).2 rfl)
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := (P.prop_triangEnvelope_iff E).1 hE
    refine ⟨m + n * (m + 1), le_antisymm ?_ ?_⟩
    · rw [hclassical]
      exact P.triangEnvelopeIter_le_triangEnvelope _
    · rw [← hn]
      have hle : ObjectProperty.singleton E ≤ P.triangEnvelopeIter m := by
        intro X hX
        obtain rfl := (ObjectProperty.singleton_iff E X).1 hX
        exact hm
      exact (ObjectProperty.monotone_triangEnvelopeIter hle n).trans
        (ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter_triangEnvelopeIter_le P m n)
  have regularToR0 : IsRegularRing R ∧ ringKrullDim R ≠ ⊤ →
      ∃ n, P.triangEnvelopeIter n = perfect := by
    rintro ⟨_, hdim⟩
    exact exists_triangEnvelopeIter_eq_isPerfect_of_isRegularRing hdim
  have r0ToRegular : (∃ n, P.triangEnvelopeIter n = perfect) →
      IsRegularRing R ∧ ringKrullDim R ≠ ⊤ := by
    intro h
    apply isRegularRing_and_ringKrullDim_ne_top_of_isStrongGenerator
    simpa [P, hclassical] using h
  exact ⟨⟨fun h => (regularToR0 h).elim fun n hn => ⟨R0, n, hn⟩, r0ToRegular ∘ toRegular⟩,
    toRegular, fun ⟨n, hn⟩ => ⟨R0, n, hn⟩⟩

end StrongGeneratorCharacterization

end StrongGeneration
